 Desktop bakes texture displacement into the volume's mesh **before** slicing;
 the slicer itself sees an ordinary mesh. Hosts call `cs_tool`
-`texture_displacement`: `meshes[0]` = the volume's base mesh (mesh-local),
-`args {layers: <Orca's texture_displacement_layers_to_json text or object>,
-images: {"<slot>": {offset, length}} (PNG bytes in the request blob),
-paint: {"<slot>": [[triangle, hex], …]} (the layer's paint mask), transform?: [16]
-mesh→world, anchor?: [x,y,z], restingDrop?: mm}` → `meshes[0]` = baked mesh,
-`result {triangles, budgetLimited}`. Then slice that mesh. Not available: the
-bake's colour output (`color_enabled` layers; it needs the GUI's palette
-quantizer).
+`texture_displacement`, then slice the returned mesh with the returned paint.
+
+```jsonc
+meshes[0]: the volume's base (undisplaced) mesh, mesh-local
+args: {
+  "layers": <texture_displacement_layers_to_json text or object {version, options, layers}>,
+                                   // options carry the colour settings: color_mix_enabled ("Mix filaments",
+                                   // default true), color_mix_count ("Mixed colors", default 8),
+                                   // color_despeckle ("Denoise", 0..6, default 2); a layer colours with color_enabled
+  "images": { "<slot>": { "offset", "length" } },   // the layer's PNG bytes in the request blob (grey or colour, 8/16-bit)
+  "paint":  { "<slot>": [[triangle, hex], …] },      // the layer's paint mask (TriangleSelector strings)
+  "transform": [16],               // optional, column-major mesh → world (instance × volume); default identity
+  "anchor": [x, y, z],             // optional world anchor (every part of a multibody object passes the same)
+  "restingDrop": 0,                // optional mm the object's lowest point lies below this volume's
+  // additive (TextureDisplacementBakeJob):
+  "volumePaint": { "support"|"seam"|"color"|"fuzzy": [[triangle, hex], …] },  // the volume's other paint
+  "modelUv": { "offset", "length" },  // optional: the model's own UV channel (ModelVolume::texture_uv), float32
+                                      // u,v × 3 per base triangle (length = triangles × 24, 4-aligned); ModelUV
+                                      // layers map through it (without it they fall back to Triplanar)
+  "color": { "config": {           // optional: turns on the "Colors" output. The project's filament slots:
+    "filament_colour": [...],      //   every slot, physical first, mixed at the tail
+    "filament_is_mixed": [...], "filament_mixed_components": [...],
+    "filament_mixed_sublayer_ratios": [...], "filament_mixed_gradient": [...] } }
+}
+→ meshes[0]: the baked mesh
+  result: {
+    "triangles", "budgetLimited", "trianglesRefined"?, "trianglesBudget"?,   // budget message numbers when limited
+    "moved": bool,                 // false: nothing displaced; desktop then keeps the paint and changes nothing
+    "topologyChanged": bool,       // the default pipeline rebuilds the mesh (pipeline_v2), the classic one does not
+    "clearSlots": [0, …],          // layer masks the commit clears (all after a rebuild, else the baked layers')
+    "paint": { "support"?, "seam"?, "color"?, "fuzzy"? },   // the volume's paint on the baked mesh: carried over
+                                   // (transfer_facet_paint) when the topology changed, the bake's colour merged
+                                   // OVER the colour paint (unpainted triangles keep the volume's own filament)
+    "colors"?: {                   // only when `color` was given and a layer colours (colour image, color_enabled)
+      "palette": [{ "color": "#RRGGBB", "a", "b", "num", "den", "filament" }],
+                                   // a = b: filament a (0-based physical); else a mix of a and b, a's share num/den;
+                                   // filament = the 0-based slot it prints in (-1 = unused mix)
+      "newMixedFilaments": [{ "slot", "components": [1-based a, b], "ratios": [a%, b%], "color" }],
+                                   // mixes the result paints with and the project has no fixed slot for
+                                   // (Sidebar::ensure_mixed_filament): append them as mixed slots, in this order,
+                                   // at these slot numbers (after every existing slot)
+      "paintedTriangles": n
+    }
+  }
+  blobs: { "triangleColor"?: uint8 per baked triangle (palette entry + 1, 0 = not coloured),
+           "modelUv"?: float32 × 6 per baked triangle (the UV channel resampled onto the new triangles) }
+```
+
+A mix is used only where it beats the nearest single filament by ΔE00 2; a
+layer whose image is made of flat colours (tiles, logos) prints in single
+filaments only (`flatColors`). The palette, its ranking of mixes (greedy over
+the colouring layers' colour histogram, every pair at ratios n/d, d ≤ 6) and
+the 24³ lookup cube are desktop's `GLGizmoTextureDisplacement` code; at most
+32 states (ExtruderMax), so `maxMixes` = 32 − physical filaments.
+
+`cs_tool` `texture_displacement_palette` is the gizmo's colour panel without
+baking: `args {layers, images, color: {config}}` (as above) → `result {layers:
+[{slot, hasColor, flatColors, flatShare}], anyColor, filaments (physical count),
+maxMixes, palette: [{color, a, b, num, den}]}` — "Colors" is offered only for a
+layer with `hasColor`; "N printable colors from M filaments" = `palette.length`
+/ `filaments`; the "Mixed colors" slider runs 1..`maxMixes`.
+
+`cs_tool` responses may carry `"blobs": {name: {offset, length}}`: named byte
+ranges of the output blob after the meshes (each 4-aligned).
+
+## Textured and coloured model import (orca 2.5, texture module)
+
+Desktop 2.5 imports glTF / GLB / FBX through Assimp, and any model that
+carries a texture, vertex colours or OBJ material colours opens the **Import
+Model** dialog: reduce the colours to a Color Count, smooth them, map each to a
+project filament (adding filaments, or mixed filaments with one-click CMYW /
+RYBW auto-mix), and the result becomes colour paint. That needs Assimp and
+OpenCV, so it lives in a **separate, lazily loaded module** next to the
+slicer, `public/wasm/texture/` (`scripts/fetch-texture-wasm.sh`):
+
+```
+texture.mjs     ES module factory (default export, EXPORT_NAME OrcaTextureModule)
+texture.wasm    single-threaded (no pthreads variant; the import runs once per model)
+texture.data    preloaded resources/filament_mixing (CMYW / RYBW recipe tables)
+version.json    {"module":"orca-texture","abi":1,"orca":"2.5.0","assimp":"5.4.3","opencv":"4.14.0","build"}
+```
+
+The slicer engine does not contain it; a host that never imports such a model
+never downloads it. Same build invariants as the engine (native Wasm EH, no
+function-pointer-cast emulation, dlmalloc, 4 GB max heap, 64 MB stack); Assimp
+(importers glTF/GLB, OBJ, FBX only, as Orca's deps) and OpenCV (core, imgproc,
+imgcodecs; PNG/JPEG through the same Emscripten ports the engine uses) are real
+libraries built by the port's toolchain.
+
+```c
+const char* tex_version(void);                   // version.json, NUL-terminated
+int  tex_call(const char* req_json, int req_len, const uint8_t* blob, int blob_len,
+              char** out_json, int* out_len, uint8_t** out_blob, int* out_blob_len);
+void tex_free(void* p);
+```
+
+`tex_call` follows `cs_tool`: request `{op, args}` + blob; response `{ok, error,
+result, meshes: [{vertexOffset, vertexCount, indexOffset, triangleCount}],
+blobs: {name: {offset, length}}}` + one output blob (meshes: float32 xyz then
+uint32 triangles; then the named blobs; each part 4-aligned). rc 0 = ok.
+Progress: `Module.csProgress(percent, message)`. A model **session** (`handle`)
+keeps the loaded textured mesh and its last analysis inside the instance (at
+most 16; `close` frees one). Filament indices are **0-based** in results, paint
+states 1-based, as everywhere. Desktop's flow, op by op:
+
+**`load`** (Model::read_from_file's textured branches; the dialog's preview data)
+```jsonc
+args: { "files": [{ "name", "offset", "length" }],   // files[0] = the model: .glb .gltf .fbx .obj; the rest are
+                                                     // what it references under their relative names (.bin,
+                                                     // .mtl, "textures/a.jpg"); no absolute paths, no ".."
+        "texturePixels": true }                      // false: skip the decoded RGBA blobs
+→ result: { "handle", "format": "glb"|"gltf"|"fbx"|"obj",
+            "importable": bool,          // desktop opens the dialog only when true (a texture with data, or
+                                         // vertex / MTL face colours); false = import the geometry as is
+            "source": "texture"|"faceColors"|null,
+            "objectTriangles", "texturedTriangles"?, "hasModelUv",
+            "materials": [{ "rgba": [r,g,b,a], "texture": index | -1 }],
+            "textures"?: [{ "width", "height", "encodedBytes", "pixels"?: blob name }] }
+  meshes[0]: the object's geometry (glTF/FBX: Assimp's triangles merged / cleaned like desktop; OBJ: Orca's
+             OBJ loader), in the FILE's frame and units (desktop then centres it and may offer a
+             metres / inches conversion; do the same and remember the transform)
+  meshes[1]: (importable) the textured mesh the analysis and the preview blobs index
+  blobs: "originalColors" uint8 RGB per textured triangle (the dialog's "Original" view: precomputed
+           colours, else sampled from the textures / material colours),
+         "uv" float32 6 per textured triangle, "faceTexture" int32 per triangle (texture index, -1 none),
+         "texture<i>" RGBA8 width×height (decoded), "modelUv" (OBJ) float32 6 per object triangle =
+           ModelVolume::texture_uv (V flipped), for Texture Displacement's ModelUV mapping
+```
+Errors: "The file format is incompatible and cannot be parsed." (Assimp),
+the OBJ loader's message, "unsupported model file".
+
+**`analyze`** (texture_to_painting / face_colors_to_painting)
+```jsonc
+args: { "handle", "colorCount": 0,      // 0 = automatic (desktop's first run), else 1..32
+        "smooth": 5,                    // 0..10 (smooth_weight = smooth / 10)
+        "repair": "ask"|"none"|"repair" }   // desktop starts with "ask"
+→ result: { "needsRepairDecision": true }   // non-manifold mesh with "ask": show desktop's choice
+                                            // ("Import without repair" → "none", "Repair and import" → "repair")
+  or      { "needsRepairDecision": false, "clusters": ["#RRGGBB"…], "clusterTriangles": [n…],
+            "colorCount", "triangles" }
+  meshes[0]: the painted mesh (subdivided / repaired; it REPLACES the object's mesh on apply)
+  blobs: "faceCluster" uint8 per painted triangle (index into clusters)
+```
+After an automatic run desktop sets the Color Count control to
+`colorCount` when it is 2..32. Errors: "Computation failed. Please adjust
+parameters and retry." (desktop falls back to a geometry-only import on the
+first run).
+
+**`match`** (do_auto_match + compaction + rows by filament, then apply_auto_standard_mix)
+```jsonc
+args: { "handle" | "clusters": ["#hex"…],
+        "filaments": [{ "color", "name"?, "type"?, "presetName"?,      // the project's slots, in order
+                        "mixed"?: bool, "components"?: "1,3"|[1,3], "ratios"?: "0.5000,0.5000"|[50,50] }],
+        "autoMerge": true,                  // "Auto-merge same filament"
+        "autoMix": "none"|"cmyw"|"rybw",    // the one-click auto-mix (none = "reset auto-mix")
+        "defaultPresetName": "" }           // preset for new filaments (desktop: the printer's
+                                            // default_filament_profile starting "Bambu PLA Basic", …)
+→ result: { "entries": [Entry…], "matches": [Match…], "dropped": bool, "autoMixApplied": bool }
+Entry: { "kind": "existing"|"existingMixed"|"new"|"newMixed", "project"?: slot (existing kinds),
+         "color", "name", "type", "presetName"?, "components"?: [1-based ENTRY indices], "ratios"?: [percent] }
+Match: { "cluster": index into clusters, "color": cluster "#hex", "filament": entry index, "deltaE" }
+```
+Entries are the dialog's filament list (existing slots first, then new ones);
+matches are its rows, in display order. Auto-merge on: each colour takes the
+nearest project filament (CIEDE2000), a new filament where ΔE > 5; off: one new
+filament per colour. Auto-mix replaces every row it has a recipe for by a new
+mixed filament of standard "Bambu PLA Basic" base colours (reusing a matching
+existing physical / mixed entry). `dropped` = the 32-filament cap was hit
+(desktop's orange warning). The host owns this state: a manual row change is
+`matches[i].filament = entry`, then pass entries + matches on.
+
+**`add_mixed`** (add_decomposed_mixed_filament: the row's colour-decompose dialog, recipe from
+`cs_tool` `mixed_filament` `recommend`)
+```jsonc
+args: { "entries", "matches", "row", "components": [{ "filament": existing physical entry } | { "color": "#hex" }],
+        "ratios": [percent…], "color": matched "#hex", "defaultPresetName"? }
+→ result: { entries, matches, dropped, autoMixApplied }   // a component colour reuses an official
+                                                         // "Bambu … Basic" entry of that colour, else a new one
+```
+
+**`apply`** (on_ok_clicked + Plater::apply_textured_mesh_import_result + apply_painted_mesh_to_volume)
+```jsonc
+args: { "handle", "entries", "matches" }      // every match must name an entry
+→ result: {
+    "newFilaments": [{ "index", "color", "presetName", "name" }],   // add as physical slots at these indices
+    "newMixedFilaments": [{ "index", "components": [1-based final], "ratios": [percent], "color" }],
+                                   // then as mixed slots (e.g. cs_tool mixed_filament expand)
+    "remap": [final slot per entry], "matches": [{ cluster, color, filament: final slot }],
+    "extruder": 1-based | null,    // the lowest filament the paint uses: the object's and the part's "extruder"
+    "paint": { "color": [[triangle, hex]…] },   // the slice job's paint.color for meshes[0]
+    "triangles" }
+  meshes[0]: the painted mesh, in the same file frame as load's meshes[0]: replace the object's (first model
+             part's) mesh with it under the transform the host gave the loaded mesh, drop to bed
+  blobs: "faceFilament" uint8 per triangle (paint state), "modelUv"? (OBJ: resampled onto the new triangles)
+```
+Unused new entries are pruned first. New physical filaments go after the
+existing physical ones, so **existing mixed slots move up** by
+`newFilaments.length` (`remap` gives their new numbers; renumber other paint
+/ extruder references to them the way adding a physical filament does); new
+mixed slots follow every existing slot. **`close`** `{handle}`.
+
+Limits: 256 input files; 32 filaments (ExtruderMax); 255 clusters per `match`.
+Not reproduced: desktop's GL preview itself (the host draws it from the blobs),
+the dialog's progress-dialog cancel (terminate the worker instead).
 
